msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:592
msgid "_Initialize array elements with C++ constructors_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:603
msgid ""
"Initialize each array element using the same C++ constructor. This operation "
"has a `body` region and an optional `partial_dtor` region. Both regions have "
"a single block whose argument is a pointer to the current array element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:608
msgid "The `body` region contains the constructor call for one element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:610
msgid ""
"The `partial_dtor` region, when non-empty, contains the destructor call for "
"one element. During lowering, it is used to build a cleanup that destroys "
"already-constructed elements if a constructor throws. When the element type "
"has a trivial destructor or exceptions are disabled, the `partial_dtor` "
"region is left empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:616 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:675
msgid ""
"When `num_elements` is absent, `addr` must be a pointer to a fixed-size CIR "
"array type and the element count is derived from that array type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:619
msgid ""
"When `num_elements` is present, `addr` is a pointer to the first element and "
"`num_elements` provides the runtime element count (for example `new T[n]`)."
msgstr ""

