#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4030
msgid ""
"It marks the point where execution of a switched-resume coroutine is "
"suspended and control returns to the caller. The result value indicates how "
"the coroutine should proceed: -1 if suspended, 0 if resumed, or 1 if "
"destroyed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4035
msgid ""
"The `id` operand is the token produced by a `cir.coro.save` that marks the "
"point when the coroutine state is prepared for suspension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4038
msgid ""
"The `final` operand indicates whether this is a final suspend point. If more "
"than one suspend point is marked final, the resume and destroy branches must "
"lead to the same basic blocks."
msgstr ""

