msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4061
msgid "`cir.coro.suspend_point` (::cir::CoroSuspendPoint)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4063
msgid "_Marks the point where a coroutine actually suspends_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4071
msgid ""
"Terminates the `suspend` region of a `cir.await`. It has no explicit "
"successors; the destination is determined by `CoroutineOp` according to how "
"the suspended coroutine is subsequently handled:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4075
msgid ""
"resume: continues execution through the `cir.await`'s `resume` region when "
"the coroutine handle is resumed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4078
msgid ""
"exit: transfers directly to the enclosing `cir.coroutine`'s `exit` region "
"when the coroutine remains suspended. The coroutine frame remains alive and "
"no cleanups are performed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4082
msgid ""
"destroy: transfers through the enclosing `cir.cleanup.scope`s to the "
"`cir.coroutine`'s `destroy` region when the coroutine handle is destroyed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4086
msgid ""
"When the optional `cond` operand is present, a `false` value vetoes the "
"suspension and control branches directly to the `resume` region of the "
"enclosing `cir.await`. A `true` value indicates the coroutine actually "
"suspends."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4091
msgid ""
"Traits: `AlwaysSpeculatableImplTrait`, `HasParent<AwaitOp>`, `Terminator`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4105
msgid "`cir.coroutine` (::cir::CoroutineOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4107
msgid "_Groups a coroutine's structured suspend/resume/destroy control flow_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4120
msgid ""
"`cir.coroutine` is an op consisting of seven regions: `initial_suspend`, "
"`body`, `final_suspend`, grp (TODO),`unwind` (TODO), `destroy`, and`exit`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4123
msgid ""
"`initial_suspend`: the coroutine ramp/setup region. Its `cir.await` marked "
"`init` is the ramp boundary: the coroutine frame and its associated state "
"are established before this point, and crossing the await transfers "
"execution to `body`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4128
msgid ""
"`body`: the user-written coroutine body, arbitrary CFG, zero or more "
"`cir.await`s at any nesting depth, terminated by `cir.co_return` or a plain "
"`cir.yield` if control simply falls off the end. This region is a structural "
"boundary separating the coroutine's setup and teardown logic (initial "
"suspend, final suspend, destroy) from the user-provided statements of the "
"original function body, including `co_await` and `co_return` expressions. In "
"particular, `cir.co_return` operations inside this region mark coroutine "
"exit points and introduce structured control flow that transfers execution "
"to `final_suspend`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4139
msgid ""
"`final_suspend`: at most one `cir.await`, marked `final`. Nothing else. "
"Corresponds to `co_await promise.final_suspend()`. Suspending at this final "
"suspend point is valid: the coroutine stays suspended until it is destroyed. "
"Resuming past this point is undefined behavior in valid programs, so its "
"`resume` edge is expected to be dead in practice, but is kept for structural "
"symmetry with the other two suspend regions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4147
msgid "`gro`: TODO."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4149
msgid "`unwind`: TODO."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4151
msgid ""
"`destroy`: destroys the coroutine frame (`coro.free` + `delete`). Reached by "
"an explicit `destroy()` call on a suspended handle, by normal completion "
"through `initial_suspend`, `final_suspend`, or by an exception escaping the "
"coroutine. Falls through to `exit` except when reached due to an escaping "
"exception, where it continues propagating that exception instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4158
msgid ""
"`exit`: the shared return-to-caller path. Reached directly from any suspend "
"point that isn't being destroyed (the coroutine is just pausing), and from "
"`destroy` when it was entered via ordinary dispatch. Holds `coro.end` + the "
"actual `cir.return`."
msgstr ""

