#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4780
msgid "`cir.eh.dispatch` (::cir::EhDispatchOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4782
msgid "_Dispatch to exception handlers based on exception type_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4793
msgid ""
"`cir.eh.dispatch` is a terminator operation that dispatches control flow "
"based on the type of the in-flight exception. It takes an `!cir.eh_token` as "
"input and branches to an eh handler block based on the exception type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4797
msgid ""
"The operation contains a list of handlers specified as type-block pairs, "
"plus either a `catch_all` handler or an `unwind` handler, which continues "
"unwinding if no catch handler matches. Exactly one of `catch_all` or "
"`unwind` must be present."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4802
msgid ""
"When the type of the in-flight exception matches a type handler, control is "
"transfered to the corresponding block with the eh_token as an argument. The "
"`catch_all` handler, if present, catches any exception not matched by "
"another type handler. The `unwind` handler is used when no handler is "
"matched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4808
msgid ""
"A handler may also be a `filter`, which carries the list of type info "
"symbols permitted by the dynamic exception specification of the enclosing "
"function. A `filter` handler has the *opposite* polarity from a `catch` "
"handler: its destination is taken when the in-flight exception is **not** "
"one of the listed types. The polarity comes from the Itanium personality "
"routine, which reports a filter failure by selecting the filter clause of "
"the landing pad. A `filter` handler therefore does not take the place of the "
"default destination, and a dispatch that has one always also has an `unwind` "
"handler, whose destination is taken when the exception is permitted. A "
"dispatch has at most one `filter` handler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4844
msgid ""
"<table>\n"
"<tr><th>Attribute</th><th>MLIR Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n"
"<tr><td><code>catch_types</code></td><td>::mlir::ArrayAttr</td><td>array "
"attribute</td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td><code>default_is_catch_all</code></td><td>::mlir::UnitAttr</"
"td><td>unit attribute</td></tr>\n"
"</table>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`default_destination`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`catch_destinations`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4865
msgid "`cir.eh.inflight_exception` (::cir::EhInflightOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4867
msgid "_Materialize the catch clause formal parameter_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4879
msgid "`cir.eh.inflight_exception` returns two values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4880
msgid "`exception_ptr`: The exception pointer for the inflight exception"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4881
msgid ""
"`type_id`: the type info index for the exception type This operation is "
"expected to be the first operation in the unwind destination basic blocks of "
"a `cir.try_call` operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4885
msgid ""
"The `cleanup` attribute indicates that clean up code must be run before the "
"values produced by this operation are used to dispatch the exception. This "
"cleanup code must be executed even if the exception is not caught. This "
"helps CIR to pass down more accurate information for LLVM lowering to "
"landingpads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4891
msgid ""
"The `catch_all` attribute indicates that a catch-all handler exists for the "
"exception being dispatched. When lowered to LLVM IR, this results in a "
"`catch ptr null` clause on the landing pad. When `catch_all` is present "
"alongside typed catches, the landing pad will contain both the typed catch "
"clauses and a trailing `catch ptr null`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4897
msgid ""
"The `filter_type_list` attribute lists the type info symbols permitted by "
"the dynamic exception specification of the enclosing function. It lowers to "
"the `filter` clause of the LLVM IR landingpad instruction. An empty list is "
"distinct from an absent one: it represents `throw()` and lowers to a zero-"
"length filter clause, which the personality routine treats as permitting "
"nothing. Since the exception specification encloses the whole function body, "
"the filter clause always comes after any catch clauses, and it terminates "
"the clause list in the same way that `catch_all` does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:4921
msgid ""
"<table>\n"
"<tr><th>Attribute</th><th>MLIR Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n"
"<tr><td><code>cleanup</code></td><td>::mlir::UnitAttr</td><td>unit "
"attribute</td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td><code>catch_all</code></td><td>::mlir::UnitAttr</td><td>unit "
"attribute</td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td><code>catch_type_list</code></td><td>::mlir::ArrayAttr</td><td>flat "
"symbol ref array attribute</td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td><code>filter_type_list</code></td><td>::mlir::ArrayAttr</td><td>flat "
"symbol ref array attribute</td></tr>\n"
"</table>\n"
msgstr ""

