#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:5154
msgid "_Handle an exception that violates an exception specification_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:5162
msgid ""
"`cir.eh.unexpected` signals that the in-flight exception violated the "
"dynamic exception specification of the enclosing function, and that "
"`std::unexpected()` must be called. The C++ standard requires this when an "
"exception that the specification does not permit tries to escape the "
"function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:5168
msgid ""
"This operation takes a `!cir.eh_token` and acts as a terminator. In high-"
"level CIR it is the only operation in the `unexpected` handler region of a "
"`cir.try` operation, where the token comes from the handler region's block "
"argument. After CFG flattening the token comes from a `cir.eh.initiate` "
"operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:5174
msgid ""
"Like `cir.eh.terminate`, this operation is ABI-agnostic. During EH ABI "
"lowering it is replaced with target-specific code. For the Itanium ABI it "
"becomes a call to `__cxa_call_unexpected` with the exception pointer, "
"followed by an unreachable operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:5197
msgid "`cir.end_catch` (::cir::EndCatchOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:5199
msgid "_End a catch handler_"
