#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6657
msgid "`cir.get_bitfield` (::cir::GetBitfieldOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6659
msgid "_Get the information for a bitfield member_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6670
msgid ""
"The `cir.get_bitfield` operation provides a load-like access to a bit field "
"of a record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6673
msgid ""
"It expects a name if a bit field, a pointer to a storage in the base record, "
"a type of the storage, a name of the bitfield, a size the bit field, an "
"offset of the bit field and a sign."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6677
msgid ""
"A unit attribute `volatile` can be used to indicate a volatile load of the "
"bitfield."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6683
msgid ""
"Example: Suppose we have a struct with multiple bitfields stored in "
"different members. The `cir.get_bitfield` operation gets the value of the "
"bitfield."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6716 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:10066
msgid ""
"<table>\n"
"<tr><th>Attribute</th><th>MLIR Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n"
"<tr><td><code>bitfield_info</code></td><td>::cir::BitfieldInfoAttr</"
"td><td>Represents info for a bit-field member</td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td><code>alignment</code></td><td>::mlir::IntegerAttr</td><td>64-bit "
"signless integer attribute</td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td><code>is_volatile</code></td><td>::mlir::UnitAttr</td><td>unit "
"attribute</td></tr>\n"
"</table>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6737
msgid "`cir.get_element` (::cir::GetElementOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6739
msgid "_Get the address of an array element_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6748
msgid ""
"The `cir.get_element` operation gets the address of a particular element "
"from the `base` array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6751
msgid ""
"It expects a pointer to the `base` array and the `index` of the element. The "
"result pointer preserves the address space of the base pointer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`base`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "pointer to array type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`index`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6791
msgid "`cir.get_global` (::cir::GetGlobalOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6793
msgid "_Get the address of a global variable_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6803
msgid ""
"The `cir.get_global` operation retrieves the address pointing to a named "
"global variable. If the global variable is marked constant, writing to the "
"resulting address (such as through a `cir.store` operation) is undefined. "
"The resulting type must always be a `!cir.ptr<...>` type with the same "
"address space as the global variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6809
msgid ""
"Addresses of thread local globals can only be retrieved if this operation is "
"marked `thread_local`, which indicates the address isn't constant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6812
msgid ""
"The `static_local` attribute indicates that this global is a function-local "
"static variable that requires guarded initialization (e.g., C++ static local "
"variables with non-constant initializers)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6827 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12649
msgid ""
"Interfaces: `ConditionallySpeculatable`, `NoMemoryEffect "
"(MemoryEffectOpInterface)`, `SymbolUserOpInterface`"
msgstr ""

