#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7118
msgid "`cir.goto` (::cir::GotoOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7126
msgid ""
"Transfers control to the specified `label`. This requires a corresponding "
"`cir.label` to exist and is used by to represent source level `goto`s that "
"jump across region boundaries. Alternatively, `cir.br` is used to construct "
"goto's that don't violate such boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7131
msgid ""
"`cir.goto` is completely symbolic (i.e. it \"jumps\" on a label that isn't "
"yet materialized) and should be taken into account by passes and analysis "
"when deciding if it's safe to make some assumptions about a given region or "
"basic block."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7175 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7612
msgid ""
"<table>\n"
"<tr><th>Attribute</th><th>MLIR Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n"
"<tr><td><code>label</code></td><td>::mlir::StringAttr</td><td>string "
"attribute</td></tr>\n"
"</table>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7182
msgid "`cir.if` (::cir::IfOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7184
msgid "_The if-then-else operation_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7186
msgid ""
"The `cir.if` operation represents an if-then-else construct for "
"conditionally executing two regions of code. The operand is a `cir.bool` "
"type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7211
msgid ""
"`cir.if` defines no values and the 'else' can be omitted. The if/else "
"regions must be terminated. If the region has only one block, the terminator "
"can be left out, and `cir.yield` terminator will be inserted implictly. "
"Otherwise, the region must be explicitly terminated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7228
msgid "`cir.inc` (::cir::IncOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7230
msgid "_Increment an integer by one_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7239
msgid ""
"The `cir.inc` operation increments the operand by one. The operand and "
"result must have the same type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7272
msgid "`cir.indirect_br` (::cir::IndirectBrOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7274
msgid "_Indirect branch_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7287
msgid ""
"The `cir.indirectbr` operation represents an indirect branch to one of "
"several possible successor blocks. The target block is computed from the "
"value of the given address operand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7291
msgid ""
"This operation is typically generated when handling constructs like the GCC "
