#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12489
msgid "_Get a the address of a virtual function pointer_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12498
msgid ""
"The `vtable.get_virtual_fn_addr` operation retrieves the address of a "
"virtual function pointer from an object's vtable (__vptr). This is an "
"abstraction to perform the basic pointer arithmetic to get the address of "
"the virtual function pointer, which can then be loaded and called."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12504
msgid ""
"The `vptr` operand must be a `!cir.ptr<!cir.vptr>` value, which would have "
"been returned by a previous call to `cir.vtable.get_vptr`. The `index` "
"operand is an index of the virtual function in the vtable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12508
msgid "The return type is a pointer-to-pointer to the function type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12551
msgid "`cir.vtable.get_vptr` (::cir::VTableGetVPtrOp)"
