"`clang::VarDecl::isLocalVarDecl()`. The namespace-scope inline variables "
"that also reach guarded initialization are not local."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13976
msgid "`tls`: the thread-local storage kind (`none`, `static`, or `dynamic`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13978
msgid ""
"`is_inline`: whether the variable is inline. Mirrors "
"`clang::VarDecl::isInline()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13981
msgid ""
"`tsk`: the template-specialization kind (`undeclared`, "
"`implicit_instantiation`, `explicit_specialization`, "
"`explicit_instantiation_declaration`, or "
"`explicit_instantiation_definition`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13993
msgid ""
"Because it stores plain data rather than a `clang::VarDecl` pointer, it "
"round-trips through textual CIR and stays valid once the AST is gone. This "
"is what lets LoweringPrepare consume these facts without a live "
"`clang::ASTContext`; the `$ast` `ASTVarDeclAttr` remains a separate, live-"
"AST handle for consumers that need arbitrary AST properties."
msgstr ""

