#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:14176
msgid "FramePointerKindAttr"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:14178
msgid "_Encodes the frame pointer kind for a function or a module._"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:14188
msgid ""
"Mirrors the `frame-pointer` function attribute and module flag of LLVM IR "
"(https://llvm.org/docs/LangRef.html#function-attributes), which tell the "
"code generator whether a function should keep its frame pointer.  The code "
"generator may keep a frame pointer even when the kind says it can be "
"eliminated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:14194
msgid ""
"`none`: the frame pointer can be eliminated, and its register can be used "
"for other purposes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:14196
msgid ""
"`reserved`: the frame pointer register must either be updated to point to a "
"valid frame record for the current function, or not be modified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:14198
msgid ""
"`non_leaf`: the frame pointer should be kept if the function calls other "
"functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:14200
msgid ""
"`non_leaf_no_reserve`: like `non_leaf`, but a leaf function may use the "
"frame pointer register for other purposes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:14202
msgid "`all`: the frame pointer should be kept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:14204
msgid ""
"On a function, the attribute applies to that function.  On the module, it "
"becomes the `frame-pointer` module flag, which LLVM applies to the functions "
"it creates after CIR is lowered, such as sanitizer constructors.  Without "
"the attribute, the kind is `none`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`::cir::FramePointerKind`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "an enum of type FramePointerKind"
msgstr ""

