"`!cir.cleanup_token` is an opaque type used to track cleanup handling state "
"in flattened CIR. It is returned by `cir.begin_cleanup` and consumed by "
"`cir.end_cleanup`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:15711
msgid ""
"This token ensures that cleanup regions are properly paired and allows the "
"ABI lowering pass to generate appropriate cleanup handling code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:15715
msgid "ComplexType"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:15717
msgid "_CIR complex type_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:15727
msgid ""
"CIR type that represents a C complex number. `cir.complex` models the C type "
"`T _Complex`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:15730
msgid "`cir.complex` type is not directly mapped to `std::complex`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:15732
msgid ""
"The type models complex values, per C99 6.2.5p11. It supports the C99 "
"complex float types as well as the GCC integer complex extensions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:15735
msgid ""
"The parameter `elementType` gives the type of the real and imaginary part of "
"the complex number. `elementType` must be either a CIR integer type or a CIR "
"floating-point type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:15750
