msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16028
msgid "Syntax: `!cir.float`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16030
msgid ""
"A 32-bit floating-point type whose format is IEEE-754 `binary32`.  It "
"represents the types `float`, `_Float32`, and `std::float32_t` in C and C++."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16034
msgid "StructType"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16036
msgid "_CIR struct/class type_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16038
msgid ""
"Each unique clang::RecordDecl with struct or class kind is mapped to a "
"`cir.struct` type.  Any object in C/C++ that has a struct or class type will "
"have a `!cir.struct` in CIR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16042 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16098
msgid "There are three possible formats:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16044 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16100
msgid "Identified and complete: unique name and a known body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16045 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16101
msgid "Identified and incomplete: unique name and unknown body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16046 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16102
msgid "Anonymous: no name and a known body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16048
msgid ""
"Typically, the full data size of a struct object is that which is calculated "
"by adding the aligned sizes of all the members. However, note that there is "
"one exception to this Flexible Array Members. When the last element is an "
"array type of size zero(in CIR), this represents the C/C++ concept of "
"'flexible array member', where as long as the type is allocated properly (or "
"a global constant), an access through the array member may access outside of "
"its bounds. This is necessary to represent C/C++ semantics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16056
msgid ""
"The optional `class` keyword distinguishes C++ class declarations from plain "
"struct declarations.  Both are semantically identical; the keyword preserves "
"the original source spelling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16060
msgid ""
"Every member has a kind, described by `CIR_RecordMemberKind`, saying what it "
"holds, and every member is spelled with its mark."
msgstr ""

